{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794589115,"nonce":"Oz16gX7zS0remjy26Do0ZB3rErc=","message":"Slice 2 landed locally in 28ecc777 (not pushed): the iOS runtimes are bundled with the macOS tarballs.\n\n- `release.yml` has an `ios-assets` job (macos-15) that builds `libash_std.a` for aarch64-apple-ios, aarch64-apple-ios-sim and x86_64-apple-ios with `cargo rustc --crate-type staticlib`, strips it, and uploads it. `package_release.sh` takes a third argument and puts each in `\u003ctriple\u003e/` beside `ash`, macOS tarballs only (only a Mac can link for iOS). A runtime that fails to build leaves its target out of the release instead of stopping it. The macOS smoke test links aarch64-apple-ios-sim from the extracted tarball.\n- Sizes, stripped: about 6.6 to 6.7 MB each, 1.9 MB gzipped.\n- Checked locally by packaging the six archives into a tarball, extracting it, and running `ash --build --target \u003ctriple\u003e` with no `--runtime` and no variables: all three iOS targets link; Mach-O platform IOS for the device, IOSSIMULATOR for both simulators, minimum 14.0; hello world on the arm64 simulator prints what the interpreter prints.\n- Fix found on the way: the link used an unversioned triple, so a device binary claimed iOS 7.0 and the x86_64 simulator failed with an undefined `start`. The link now uses the same versioned triple as the object.\n\nNot run anywhere yet: the new CI jobs (they run when pushed). Item 3 is now met for all three targets pending that run. Still open: the static library / XCFramework form, entry glue, `ash run`, CI for device runs, static native binding.","files":null}]}